# hh Policy Pack (F1)

## Privacy Defaults

- Strict mode is default: no raw audio retention, no transcript persistence.
- Never log or persist user transcripts or audio payloads unless debug mode is explicitly enabled.
- Redact secrets in all log output; omit sensitive values when logging config.

## Approval Gates

- High-impact actions (pr_create, code_change) require explicit approval gates.
- Do not bypass policy checks; denied actions must block with actionable reasons.
- Use the approval gates module (`approvalGates`) for high-impact action checks.

## Testing Expectations

- Every new module must have corresponding tests.
- Tests must cover success, timeout, cancel, and transient failure paths where applicable.
- Run `npm test` before committing; all tests must pass.

## Minimal-Diff Discipline

- Prefer smallest safe change; avoid unnecessary churn.
- Preserve architectural boundaries; do not cross module boundaries without explicit contracts.
- When adding features, follow existing patterns in the codebase.
